    "3": {
      "note": "No history or overwrite payload: `record_payloads` returns complete fresh source units for missing or resumable records only. When a companion is missing, exact present members remain in the payload so the transaction checks the whole unit, skips equal writes and includes those held members in refusal-versus-HEAD reporting; differing existing bytes are refused. Apply must reopen indexes/replan to catch relocated identity conflicts. Source history has reading_aid_only=True and is never a payload or a recovery-curator row. These helpers perform no writes; the caller owns the transaction.",
